<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_DustHusk.xml                        RimMandrake — COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1

  Resolves ledger slug
  `dune_sea+deep_desert:dormancy-trigger-dune-fauna-reskin-lane-107-live-vfei2-dorma`
  (dune_sea.md SS4: "there is no circadian clock anywhere in this biome...
  life here is event-driven. The default state of the dune sea is
  dormancy... What ends dormancy is not a time of day; it is a trigger —
  free water, a vibration, a temperature anomaly, blood."; deep_desert.md
  SS4 "Anhydrobiosis: some things dry to dust and wait... and rehydrate."
  roster's own new_defs entry (rosters/dune_sea_deep_desert.json):
  mechanic_load "reskin, no new C#" — "reskin lane: 107 live VFEI2 dormant
  rows carry the mechanic" (`_assignment_prep.md` SS1.4: "Dormancy-triggered
  forms: donor mechanic EXISTS — 107 live rows carry 'lies dormant until
  something wakes it' (mostly VFE-Insectoids 2) — candidates for reskin
  into trigger-on-water/vibration dune fauna rather than new C#").

  The "107 live rows" point at PRECEDENT, not a specific donor to graft
  onto: the mechanic itself is the STOCK vanilla comp pair
  (`CompProperties_CanBeDormant`/`CompProperties_WakeUpDormant`), the same
  pair `RUT_SealedSleeper` (this item, the_cracked_lands wave) already
  proved out and read in full from RimWorld/CompWakeUpDormant.cs — no
  VFEI2 dependency is needed or taken (checked cast_assignment.csv/
  animal_census.csv first: no VFEI2 species is cast to this biome and none
  is absorbed into our own RSW_/RUT_ namespace, so grafting a live
  ThingDef from that mod via ParentName would introduce a new, untested
  cross-mod inheritance shape this item has never used elsewhere — the
  stock-comp route is both cheaper and matches the roster's own "no new
  C#" line exactly).

  RM_-tier, not RUT_: this is invented content with no Star Wars flavor at
  all, so per Q11a it belongs franchise-free in `mandrake.rm.stillsand`
  directly (same reasoning as `RM_MirrorGiant`, authored this same pass) —
  not routed through `WildAnimals_Stillsand.xml`, which exists only to
  replay content copied off the frozen `RUT_ExtremeDesert.xml` twin.

  `wakeUpOnDamage=true` only (blood — one of dune_sea.md's own three named
  triggers, "free water, a vibration, a temperature anomaly, blood").
  Vibration/water-specific waking is the SAME stock-class gap
  `RUT_SealedSleeper`'s header already measured ("no water/terrain-type
  targeting exists in the stock class") — that half is NOT invented here;
  it stays real future C# if the owner wants it (parallel posture to
  `CRACKED_LANDS_SEALED_WAKE_MECHANISM_1`, not re-filed as its own item
  since dune_sea.md never singles out ONE specific wake-trigger species the
  way the_cracked_lands.md's Sealed does — a plain damage-wake dormant
  organism already satisfies this slug's own "reskin, no new C#" ask as
  written).

  Body: grain-scale per dune_sea.md SS4's bimodal law ("giants on the
  surface, and grain-scale life below it, with a hard gap where every
  ordinary animal would be") — bodySize 0.15, scaled off the census's own
  VFEI2_Boomtick reference point (bs 0.18, the smallest unclaimed VFEI2 row
  checked this pass, used only as a scale reference — no VFEI2 asset or
  def reused, same "dormant-status/live-but-unabsorbed donor as scale
  reference only" precedent this item has used repeatedly). Vanilla
  QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail body, same body RUT_SealedSleeper used —
  no new BodyDef, no external dependency.

  Art: genuinely new, no existing render found for "dust husk"/
  "dormant"/"husk" tied to this biome (checked infrastructure/artpipe/
  {done,pending,registry.jsonl} this pass — clean, only unrelated hits).
  Three facing jobs filed, rmdusthusk_v1_{south,east,north} — prompt
  written per SS4's own pigment law ("bright white is the dayside's
  pigment") and SS6's ban on shine/crystal look (desiccated, matte, dusty,
  never glassy).

  🔴 THE NAME IS NOT SETTLED — RM_DustHusk is the INTERNAL working
  defName, same posture RUT_SealedSleeper/RUT_MortuaryCrawler used. Filed
  STILLSAND_SHIPPING_NAMES_1 this pass to cover it, alongside RM_MirrorGiant.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_DustHusk</defName>
    <label>dust husk</label>
    <description>A grain-scale animal that spends most of its existence as dry, motionless dust wedged between sand grains — not dormant in the way a sleeper is dormant, but genuinely desiccated, its whole metabolism banked to nothing. A sandstorm can carry thousands of them aloft as an ordinary-looking dust cloud, and most of what looks like empty sand out here is actually a field of them, waiting. Only real damage rouses one; nothing else out here is worth the water it would cost to wake for.</description>
    <receivesSignals>true</receivesSignals>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>1.2</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>0.4</Mass>
      <MarketValue>12</MarketValue>
      <Wildness>0.9</Wildness>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>999</ComfyTemperatureMax>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>mandible</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>3</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.6</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_CanBeDormant">
        <startsDormant>true</startsDormant>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_WakeUpDormant">
        <!-- Stock comp pair (RUT_SealedSleeper precedent, this item). Only
             "blood" (damage) is wired here — see header for why the
             vibration/water triggers dune_sea.md also names stay
             unbuilt-and-unclaimed rather than invented. -->
        <wakeUpOnDamage>true</wakeUpOnDamage>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail</body>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <baseBodySize>0.15</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.3</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.05</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>OmnivoreRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <roamMtbDays>60</roamMtbDays>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <lifeExpectancy>15</lifeExpectancy>
      <gestationPeriodDays>6</gestationPeriodDays>
      <litterSizeCurve>
        <points>
          <li>(0.5, 0)</li>
          <li>(1, 1)</li>
          <li>(2, 0.4)</li>
          <li>(3, 0)</li>
        </points>
      </litterSizeCurve>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.1</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.25</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Herbivore_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalExotic</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_DustHusk</defName>
    <label>dust husk</label>
    <labelPlural>dust husks</labelPlural>
    <race>RM_DustHusk</race>
    <combatPower>4</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>1~3</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.2</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_DustHusk/RM_DustHusk</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.3</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_DustHusk/RM_DustHusk</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.4</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_DustHusk/RM_DustHusk</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.5</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
